<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

  <parent>
    <groupId>org.cometgui</groupId>
    <artifactId>cometgui-parent</artifactId>
    <version>0.1.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
  </parent>

  <artifactId>cometgui-workflow</artifactId>
  <packaging>jar</packaging>
  <name>CometGUI :: Workflow engine</name>
  <description>The stage DAG, its explicit states, and the orchestration of validate, Comet, Percolator and the downstream stages.</description>

  <!--
    THE MUTATION GATE IS ON IN THIS MODULE (phase 02 unit 3).
    The parent POM lists org.cometgui.workflow.state.* among PIT's
    <targetClasses> because R-TEST-02 counts the stage state model as critical
    pure logic, and phase 02 unit 3 put the first classes into that package.
    The threshold itself (80%) lives in the parent POM so that no module can
    hold a different number.
    Setting this back to true to make a build pass is a weakening of a gate and
    is rejected at sign-off; so is removing the package from <targetClasses>.

    cometgui.coverage.core.skip is deliberately NOT set here.  That switch
    applies the 90% line / 85% branch rule to the whole module bundle, and this
    module is where phase 08's workflow engine will land; committing the engine
    to that number is not this phase's call to make.  The coverage of what is
    here is measured and reported at every build all the same - scripts/build.sh
    prints it - and the phase that adds the engine owns the decision.
  -->
  <properties>
    <cometgui.mutation.skip>false</cometgui.mutation.skip>
  </properties>

  <!--
    Only the edges the specification's layering permits are declared here.
    Adding one is an architectural change: say so in the phase handoff, and
    expect the ArchUnit rules in cometgui-archtests to have an opinion.
  -->
  <dependencies>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.cometgui</groupId>
      <artifactId>cometgui-domain</artifactId>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.cometgui</groupId>
      <artifactId>cometgui-tools</artifactId>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.cometgui</groupId>
      <artifactId>cometgui-provenance</artifactId>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.cometgui</groupId>
      <artifactId>cometgui-results</artifactId>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.cometgui</groupId>
      <artifactId>cometgui-params-comet</artifactId>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.cometgui</groupId>
      <artifactId>cometgui-params-percolator</artifactId>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>
  <build>
    <plugins>
      <!--
        WHY THIS MODULE'S TESTS FORCE A UTF-8 LOCALE ON THE FORKED JVM (phase 14
        unit 8a), for the reason cometgui-process gives in full.

        The specification's failure-path list names "paths containing Unicode",
        and RealAwkwardPathRunTest proves it through this module's workflow with
        the real Comet and Percolator.  The build host exports no locale, so a
        JVM forked here reports sun.jnu.encoding=ANSI_X3.4-1968 and cannot
        spell a non-ASCII file name at all; measured before this block was
        added, that test FAILED by design ("expected: <UTF-8> but was:
        <ANSI_X3.4-1968>"), under surefire and in PIT's coverage run alike
        ("1 tests did not pass without mutation").  pitest-maven reads this
        block from surefire's configuration, so one setting serves both; PIT's
        own configuration is not touched.

        A TEST ENVIRONMENT correction, not a weakened gate: the test still
        asserts the encoding and fails, never skips, without it.  Tools are
        unaffected - the process service clears a tool's environment and puts
        back only what the command names - so no product launch sees LANG.
      -->
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
        <configuration>
          <environmentVariables>
            <LANG>C.UTF-8</LANG>
            <LC_ALL>C.UTF-8</LC_ALL>
          </environmentVariables>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
</project>
